<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48138" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεμόω</span></b> , only in phrase [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆα] θέμωσε . . χέρσον ἱκέσθαι</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>drove</i> the ship <i>ashore,
				stranded</i> her, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.486
			</span></i>; but in ib.<i><span class="en">
				542
			</span></i>, <i>drove</i> her landwards, i.e. towards her destination:
			cf. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεμούς:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαθέσεις, παραινέσεις</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, who also has <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεμῶν:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θελήμων</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
